# A popover behind-click is a DISMISSAL, so an ask row cannot be focused
# underneath one.
#
# WHAT THIS USED TO ASSERT, AND WHY IT COULD NOT. It focused ask_option_q1_0,
# pressed SPACE and ENTER, and required the card untouched. Two things were
# wrong with that. afterhours' imm::popover takes the open flag by REFERENCE and
# closes itself when focus leaves, so `focus_ui` on a row behind the popover
# dismisses it -- measured at the SPACE frame, modelPopoverOpen was already 0,
# so no overlay owned anything. And ask_keys_live needs the card focused, so the
# two halves of the old premise are mutually exclusive: there is no state in
# which a popover is up AND the card holds the keyboard. It passed anyway
# because ENTER on a focused row un-picked the option (the S1 defect) and put
# the "Answer any one of these" note back, which is the text it asserted.
#
# What IS true and worth guarding is the dismissal itself. Both assertions are
# live: the first fails if the overlay never opened, the second if reaching
# behind it left it up.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_ASK_DEMO=1 HANABI_TEST_OVERLAY=model

require_thread t2
expect_text "The agent is asking"
expect_text "Default for new tasks"

focus_ui ask_option_q1_0
wait_frames 12
expect_no_text "Default for new tasks"
